      "title": "Value Chain Adjunct Faculty",
      "description": "Value Chain Adjunct Faculty Location York, PA Job Type Faculty, Part Time Job Number 202600131 Division Graham School of Business Department Operations and Information Technology Opening Date 11/17/2026 Closing Date 12/7/2026 11:59 PM Eastern Description Benefits Questions Position Summary Job Description: We are seeking a knowledgeable and experienced Value Chain Adjunct Faculty to teach face-to-face sections of SCM100 (Modern Value Chain) during the fall 2027 semester. The instructor will deliver engaging and practical instruction aligned with industry standards. Responsibilities include preparing course materials, facilitating class discussions, assessing student performance, and supporting learners in achieving academic success. The ideal candidate will bring value chain experience, strong communication skills, and a commitment to student learning. Outcome: Hiring an adjunct faculty member to teach SCM100 (Modern Value Chain) and possibly other courses. Essential Functions Teach face-to-face SCM100 (Modern Value Chain) classes in fall 2027. May also have opportunities to teach other undergraduate and/or graduate classes in the future. The specific courses will vary from semester to semester and the availability of courses to teach depends on the needs of the GSB. Prepare course materials, assess student performance, and provide timely feedback to students. Communicate effectively with and support students, which includes making use of our learning management system. Adjunct faculty who are teaching courses are required to hold one office hour on campus each week. Experience and Education Required Master’s or doctorate degree in supply chain management or a closely related field. Required Skills and Qualifications Professional value chain/supply chain experience (e.g., purchasing, operations, distribution) required. Prior teaching experience at the college level preferred. The preferred candidate will be able to teach during the day. Additional Information York College of Pennsylvania is an Equal Opportunity Employer and Non-Discriminatory . For a copy of York College's Annual Security Report, you may contact the Office of Campus Safety or visit the website: Annual Security Report . Part-time employees are eligible to make elective retirement contributions on a pretax basis as described in the college's Retirement Benefit Plan. To learn more details, visit our benefits page . 01 Are you available to teach face-to-face classes in York, PA starting in August 2027? Yes No 02 Do you have a Master’s or Doctorate degree in Supply Chain Management or a closely related field? Yes No 03 Do you have professional value chain/supply chain experience? Yes No 04 Do you have experience teaching in a collegiate setting? Yes No 05 Are you available to teach during the day (between 8 AM and 5 PM)? Yes No 06 Are you legally eligible to work in the US without employer sponsorship? Yes No Required Question Employer York College of Pennsylvania Address 441 Country Club Road York, Pennsylvania, 17403 Phone 717-815-1320 Website https://www.ycp.edu/ Apply"
